From c7c9133f7c059d3e3ef4a6d51ed56d23da306c3c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:47:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Reaper UI: guest portal look fixed, Network and AiMesh
 restyle, device pictures, tall dialogs, add-on sheet, quiet frame

- Network page (REAPER-NET-FF385): the guest portal look is asked by the right hook name, so the saved background,
  title and terms load again and a save no longer writes the built-in look over them; the look is uploaded only when
  it was loaded, is new or was changed. Live phone preview of the portal, also in the wizard. Wi-Fi key, RADIUS
  secret and portal passcode are masked with Show / Hide; the Share dialog masks the key on screen. The MAC filter
  lists each device as Name (MAC) with a picker of the wireless devices online. Cards say the kind of network and
  Secured / Open. Final restyle in the Reaper colours.
- Devices (REAPER-DEVICON): an icon per device (its picture, else its type, else a generic one) and a dialog to
  upload or remove a picture and pick the type; the same icons on the dashboard and AiMesh client lists.
- AiMesh: final restyle; the backhaul card shows Maximum (the negotiated link rate) and every traffic figure is on
  its own line (REAPER-AIMESH-RATES).
- Dialogs (REAPER-DLG-TALL): a dialog taller than the visible part of the page is pinned in the page and the frame
  grows to hold it, so the page scrollbar reaches its buttons; no dialog has a height cap in viewport units or a
  scrollbar of its own (Devices, Network, AiMesh, Wi-Fi schedule). The Devices picture dialog uses the window width.
- Add-on pages: new reaper/reaper_addon.css hides the stock banner, menu and tabs and gives the page the Reaper
  colours; the shell applies it as a backstop.
- Kit frame: the band around a page's sections is neutral with a thin accent line instead of the crimson fill.
- System page: the ASUS Router app switch (Login and access), with the trade-off stated.
- Wireless Log: Rx / Tx retries column.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
